<!--
  Symphony No. 5 in C minor, Op. 67, first movement, by Ludwig van Beethoven: written music for HumanityOS's score player (docs/design/score-player.md).
  Source: https://www.mutopiaproject.org/cgibin/piece-info.cgi?id=941 (Symphony5_1-lys.zip, SHA-256 a0165591776ac4f277ff4331b075774d739639726f26f162aad57761554abf80; each file's own SHA-256 is in scripts/ly-to-mei.pieces.json).
  Edition: Breitkopf & Härtel, 1862-1865. Licence: public domain (docs/reference/findings/2026-11-20-public-domain-scores.md, finding 20).
  Converted by scripts/ly-to-mei.js. Tempo numbers are not printed in this edition: Allegro con brio plays at a half note = 108 (216 quarter notes a minute), Beethoven's own metronome mark as the Allgemeine musikalische Zeitung printed it on 17 December 1817 (docs/reference/findings/2026-11-20-beethoven-5-metronome.md); the oboe's Adagio cadenza, which has no mark of his, plays at 60 quarter notes a minute, our own playback choice, and the Allegro again after it; these are playback values (midi.bpm), the words are the edition's.
  The double basses sound an octave below the written notes (trans.semi -12), as the instrument does; the clarinets in B flat and the horns in E flat are written as they read them (trans.semi -2 and -9).
  Open it in MuseScore 4.2 or later, or any text editor; change a note and the game plays the change the next time the piece starts.
-->
<mei xmlns="http://www.music-encoding.org/ns/mei" meiversion="5.1+basic">
